    ("gov_m2_25", "Nationalism: Zikist Movement", "2011", "The Zikist Movement formed in 1946 was characterized by its philosophy of:", ["Militant, radical nationalism and positive direct action against colonialism", "Unconditional cooperation with colonial authorities", "Restricting political agitation to Lagos only", "Monarchical traditionalism"], 0, "The Zikist Movement (founded by Kola Balogun, Nduka Eze, Mokwugo Okoye, etc.) adopted revolutionary and radical methods against colonial oppression.", "Medium"),
    ("gov_m2_26", "Nationalism: NYM Crisis 1941", "2012", "The disintegration of the Nigerian Youth Movement (NYM) in 1941 was precipitated by the contest between:", ["Ernest Ikoli and Samuel Akinsanya", "Herbert Macaulay and Nnamdi Azikiwe", "Obafemi Awolowo and Ahmadu Bello", "Tafawa Balewa and Aminu Kano"], 0, "The vacant Legislative Council seat contest between Ernest Ikoli and Samuel Akinsanya triggered ethnic splits and the resignation of Azikiwe and Western/Eastern factions.", "Medium"),
    ("gov_m2_27", "Constitutional Development: 1957 Self-Government", "2014", "Internal self-government was granted to the Eastern and Western Regions in:", ["1957", "1959", "1960", "1954"], 0, "The Western and Eastern Regions attained internal self-government in 1957, while the Northern Region followed in 1959.", "Easy"),
