    ("gov_m2_41", "Nationalism: NPC Foundation", "2012", "The Northern People's Congress (NPC) originated from a Northern cultural organization called:", ["Jam'iyyar Mutanen Arewa", "Northern Elements Progressive Association", "Borno Youth Movement", "United Middle Belt Congress"], 0, "The NPC evolved in 1951 from the Jam'iyyar Mutanen Arewa (Society of the People of the North) formed by Dr. Dikko, Yahaya Gusau, and Aminu Kano.", "Easy"),
    ("gov_m2_42", "Nationalism: NEPU", "2013", "The Northern Elements Progressive Union (NEPU) was founded in 1950 by Mallam Aminu Kano to:", ["Champion the rights of the common masses (Talakawa) against feudal oppression", "Preserve the autocratic powers of the Native Authorities", "Abolish Islamic Sharia law", "Merge the North into the Western Region"], 0, "NEPU was a radical populist movement fighting for the democratic empowerment and emancipation of the Talakawa.", "Easy"),
    ("gov_m2_43", "Constitutional Development: 1950 Ibadan Conference", "2014", "The 1950 Ibadan General Conference was convened primarily to:", ["Review the Richards Constitution and formulate proposals for a new constitution", "Declare sovereign independence for Nigeria", "Draft the first military penal code", "Elect the first Prime Minister of the Federation"], 0, "The Ibadan Conference brought together representatives from all provinces and regions to draft what became the 1951 Macpherson Constitution.", "Medium"),
    ("gov_m2_44", "Colonial Administration: Assimilation vs Association", "2011", "When the French colonial policy of assimilation faced severe resistance and proved impractical, it was replaced with the policy of:", ["Association", "Direct Rule", "Paternalism", "Indirect Rule"], 0, "France transitioned from rigid assimilation to 'association', which respected indigenous customs while maintaining French control.", "Easy"),
    ("gov_m2_45", "Pre-Colonial Systems: Nupe Etsu", "2014", "The traditional monarch and supreme political ruler of the Nupe Kingdom is titled the:", ["Etsu Nupe", "Attah of Igala", "Aku Uka of Wukari", "Tor Tiv"], 0, "The Etsu Nupe is the royal sovereign of the Nupe Kingdom based in Bida.", "Easy"),
