    ("gov_m2_47", "Colonial Administration: Divide and Rule", "2012", "The British colonial strategy of preventing united anti-colonial political action among Nigerian ethnic nationalities is described as:", ["Divide and rule", "Policy of assimilation", "Enfranchisement", "Indirect federation"], 0, "Divide and rule kept regions, ethnic groups, and administrations segregated to prevent collective resistance against colonial authority.", "Easy"),
    ("gov_m2_48", "Nationalism: WASU 1925", "2014", "The West African Students' Union (WASU) was founded in London in 1925 by:", ["Ladipo Solanke", "Herbert Macaulay", "Kwami Nkrumah", "H.O. Davies"], 0, "Chief Ladipo Solanke from Nigeria, alongside Dr. Bankole-Bright from Sierra Leone, founded WASU to mobilize student nationalism in Britain.", "Medium"),
